## 3. Verification and Quality Metrics

NegoSphere includes dedicated verification scripts for important negotiation and reporting workflows. The project records identify the following verification areas:

| Verification area | Project check | What it is intended to validate |
|---|---|---|
| Core negotiation | `npm run verify:negotiation` | Core negotiation rules and outcomes. |
| Scenario regression | `npm run verify:all-scenarios` | Behavior across the predefined scenario set. |
| Practice Mode | `npm run verify:practice` | Practice Mode negotiation behavior. |
| Practice orchestration | `npm run verify:practice-orchestrator` | Integration with the negotiation orchestrator. |
| Human offer decisions | `npm run verify:practice-decisions` | Practice Mode acceptance and rejection decisions. |
| Negotiation analysis | `npm run verify:negotiation-analysis` | Negotiation analysis and insights. |
| Strategic negotiation | `npm run verify:strategic-negotiation` | Strategic negotiation constraints and behavior. |
| Report integrity | `npm run verify:report-integrity` | Consistency between negotiation outcomes and report data. |
| Dashboard performance | `npm run verify:dashboard-performance` | Dashboard performance-related checks. |

These scripts are available in the project configuration. Their presence does not, by itself, prove that every script passed in the current checkout. Record the date, command, exit status, and relevant output whenever each check is run.

### Release checks that must be reported separately

| Check | Command | Reporting requirement |
|---|---|---|
| Frontend production build | `npm run build` | Record success or failure from an actual run. |
| Lint | `npm run lint` | Record warnings and errors, not just the exit status. |
| Negotiation verification | Relevant `verify:*` scripts | Record each script's individual result. |
| Python backend tests | `python -m pytest` from the configured backend environment, if applicable | Record collected, passed, failed, and skipped tests. |
| Backend health | Check the configured health endpoint while the backend is running | Record actual response and service configuration. |
| Integration test | Start the required services and test a complete workflow | Record the workflow, environment, and outcome. |

A passing targeted verification script should not be represented as proof that the complete frontend build, every integration, all external AI providers, or deployment have passed.

