## 7. Overall Sprint Review

NegoSphere's Agile work is organized around building and validating a complete negotiation-training workflow: scenario selection, agent configuration, negotiation orchestration, simulation and practice, learning analysis, reporting, user history, and platform integration.

The project's dedicated verification scripts provide a basis for repeatable quality checks. The most important continuing priorities are realistic negotiation decisions, accurate transcripts and outcomes, learning explanations grounded in session data, consistent report exports, and clear release verification.

Sprint velocity, completion percentages, defect totals, test pass rates, and claims of production readiness should be added only when supported by the team's actual records.

### Final Reporting Note

This document deliberately does not invent a total story-point count, 100% completion rate, defect totals, or a universal test pass rate. The available NegoSphere materials do not establish those aggregate figures. Populate the metrics tables from the team's sprint tracker and actual test outputs before using them as measured results in an academic submission.
